📊 Statistical Analysis of Ola Ride Booking Performance Using Python
________________________________________
Business Problem
Ola processes over 103,000 ride bookings, generating large volumes of operational data covering booking status, cancellations, ride completion, payment methods, vehicle types, ride distance, customer ratings, and booking values. However, operations teams often rely on descriptive dashboards without statistically validating whether observed differences are meaningful or simply random variation.
This project applies inferential statistics to identify the operational factors that significantly influence booking outcomes and revenue, enabling data-driven improvements to ride fulfillment, cancellation reduction, and customer experience.
________________________________________
Business Objectives
This project was designed to answer the following business questions:
•	Does booking value differ across booking statuses, vehicle types, payment methods, or ride outcomes? 
•	Does the day of the week significantly influence booking value? 
•	Does ride distance affect booking revenue? 
•	Which ride outcomes contribute most to overall booking value? 
•	Are customer and driver ratings correlated? 
•	Which operational variables are associated with one another? 
•	Which business areas should Ola prioritize to reduce cancellations and improve revenue? 
________________________________________
Project Description
Performed an end-to-end statistical analysis on 103,024 ride bookings using Python, Power BI and SQL to evaluate the impact of ride status, booking status, vehicle type, payment method, ride distance, booking day, and operational outcomes on booking performance. Applied 20+ statistical hypothesis tests, including Kruskal–Wallis, Independent Samples T-Test, Chi-Square Goodness-of-Fit, Chi-Square Test of Independence, Correlation Analysis, and Bonferroni post-hoc analysis, to distinguish statistically significant operational drivers from random variation and provide evidence-based recommendations for improving ride completion and customer experience.
________________________________________
